{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Execute Next Task : Build Sequence Orchestrator",
  "description": "Monitors build-sequence/tasks.md for changes and orchestrates task execution by enforcing correct order, delegating to service-level specs, and maintaining STATUS.md with minimal progress updates (last task, timestamp, single note). Uses Gemini search when needed for information.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "The build-sequence/tasks.md file. You are the high-level orchestrator responsible for:\n\n1. **Enforce Execution Order**: Review the task list and ensure tasks are executed in the correct sequence as defined in build-sequence/tasks.md\n2. **Delegate to Service Specs**: For each task, delegate detailed implementation to the corresponding service-level specification files (do not implement details yourself)\n3. **Mark Completion**: When a task is complete, mark it as completed in build-sequence/tasks.md and update the status of all linked service-level tasks\n4. **Update STATUS.md**: After every task completion, update STATUS.md with ONLY:\n   - The last task completed\n   - The timestamp\n   - A single essential progress note\n   Keep it minimal - no extra details in STATUS.md\n5. **Use Gemini Search**: If you need information to make decisions, use Gemini search\n6. **Work Thoughtfully**: Execute tasks with careful consideration and attention to detail\n\nReview the current state of build-sequence/tasks.md, identify the next task to execute, delegate appropriately, and maintain the status tracking. "
  }
}